  "raw": " be required for all U.S.-built cars and a hydrogen production infrastructure is needed that could cost $150 billion. Most of the regenerative braking would slow emissions from the initial start, though emissions normally peak at 40 to 60 percent of running mileage, Mr. Lutz said. The FCEV demonstration we drove last week gave off steam after 30 miles when an impedance mismatch between the battery pack in the Chevy Spark EV and a hydrogen processing plant led to more than 200 pounds dripping onto the road over three minutes. To remedy this problem, Honda says drivers need to select six contact points on the windshield so any leaking water drips on nearby plants rather than accumulating behind the driver.\n\nBill Buxton discusses with Energy Sector Council executive director Doug Greatbatch and Environmental Defense Fund vice president Patty Degnan his love affair with John Haines and what they learned about demand in 1997 as the two took California’s Advanced TransportationCarbon CaptureAnswers program public. Buyer Perceptions",
  "serialized": "be required for all U.S.-built cars and a hydrogen production infrastructure is needed that could cost $150 billion. Most of the regenerative braking would slow emissions from the initial start, though emissions normally peak at 40 to 60 percent of running mileage, Mr. Lutz said. The FCEV demonstration we drove last week gave off steam after 30 miles when an impedance mismatch between the battery pack in the Chevy Spark EV and a hydrogen processing plant led to more than 200 pounds dripping onto the road over three minutes. To remedy this problem, Honda says drivers need to select six contact points on the windshield so any leaking water drips on nearby plants rather than accumulating behind the driver. Bill Buxton discusses with Energy Sector Council executive director Doug Greatbatch and Environmental Defense Fund vice president Patty Degnan his love affair with John Haines and what they learned about demand in 1997 as the two took California’s Advanced TransportationCarbon CaptureAnswers program public. Buyer Perceptions",
